[Demo/README.md] # C# Basics — Workshop 02 Demo

Companion code for `Week03_Basics.pptx` and `Week03_Questions_Bank.pptx` (.NET Track).

Target framework: **net8.0** · `ImplicitUsings` **disabled** (every `using` is written out) · `Nullable` **enabled**.

## Structure

```
Workshop02Demo.sln
├── CSharpBasicsLib/                 class library — all user-defined types + model answers
│   ├── Arrays/ArrayTasks.cs         Q1 – Q5
│   ├── Functions/FunctionTasks.cs   Q6 – Q8
│   ├── NullSafety/NullTasks.cs      Q9 – Q10
│   ├── Types/UserDefinedTypes.cs    Q11 – Q13  (Grade, Permission, Point)
│   └── RefValue/RefValueTasks.cs    Q14 – Q19
└── Workshop02.ConsoleApp/           console app — references the library
    ├── Program.cs                   menu
    ├── AnswerKey.cs                 runs all 19 questions with the slide's sample data
    └── Demos/                       one file per slide topic
        ├── ArrayDemo.cs
        ├── ParameterPassingDemo.cs
        ├── NullSafetyDemo.cs
        ├── TypesDemo.cs
        └── EnumsDemo.cs
```

## Run it

```bash
dotnet run --project Workshop02.ConsoleApp
```

Or open `Workshop02Demo.sln` in Visual Studio, set **Workshop02.ConsoleApp** as the startup project, and press F5.

## Menu

| Option | What it shows | Slide |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `Array.Sort / Reverse / IndexOf / Fill`, the `Resize` trap, the `Clone` shallow-copy trap, 1D vs 2D vs jagged | Array Class & Array Methods · 1D / 2D / Jagged |
| 2 | value · `ref` · `out` · `in` · `params`, then value type vs reference type | Parameter Passing · Value vs Reference |
| 3 | `Nullable<int>` internals, NRT warnings, `?.` `??` `??=` `!` | Nullable Types · Null Operators |
| 4 | copy vs share, equality, `with` expressions, nullability | Class vs Struct vs Record |
| 5 | underlying types, `Parse` vs `TryParse`, `IsDefined`, `[Flags]` bitwise combine / remove | Enums Deep Dive · [Flags] Enums |
| 6 | every question's expected output | Questions Bank |

## Notes for the session

* **No overloading and no interfaces anywhere** — every method has a unique name, matching what the students have covered so far.
* `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture` is set in `Main` so decimals always print as `5.5`, whatever the machine's regional settings are.
* Three commented lines are there on purpose, to be uncommented live so the class sees the compiler error:
  * `ParameterPassingDemo.ShowReadOnly` — assigning to an `in` parameter.
  * In `RefValueTasks.Track`, change `ref` to `out` and show it will not compile.
  * In `FunctionTasks.GetStats`, delete one `out` assignment and show the error.
* The answer key uses **Example 1** from each slide, so you can project the question and the expected output side by side while correcting.

