Companion code for `Week04_Basics.pptx` and `Week04_Questions_Bank.pptx` (.NET Track).

Target framework: **net8.0** · `ImplicitUsings` **disabled** (every `using` is written out) · `Nullable` **enabled**.

## Structure

```
Workshop03Demo.sln
├── ArraysEnumsLib/                        class library
│   ├── ArrayFunctions/ArrayFunctionTasks.cs   Q1 – Q3   (must use the Array class)
│   ├── ArrayExamples/ArrayExampleTasks.cs     Q4 – Q5   (must NOT use the Array class)
│   ├── Jagged/JaggedTasks.cs                  Q6 – Q7
│   └── Permissions/PermissionTasks.cs         Q8        ([Flags] enum lives here)
└── Workshop03.ConsoleApp/
    ├── Program.cs                         menu
    ├── AnswerKey.cs                       runs all 8 questions with the slide's sample data
    └── Demos/
        ├── ArrayFunctionsDemo.cs
        ├── ArrayExamplesDemo.cs
        ├── JaggedArrayDemo.cs
        └── PermissionDemo.cs
```

## Run it

```bash
dotnet run --project Workshop03.ConsoleApp
```

Or open `Workshop03Demo.sln` in Visual Studio, set **Workshop03.ConsoleApp** as the startup project, and press F5.

## Menu

| Option | What it shows | Slide |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | the slide example line by line, `Copy` vs `CopyTo`, why `Resize` needs `ref` | Array Functions · Copy / CopyTo / Resize |
| 2 | `for` vs `foreach`, reverse with two pointers, max without `Array.Sort`, move zeros | Walking an Array · More Examples |
| 3 | the three ways to build `int[][]`, the null-row trap, jagged vs 2D syntax, marks per student | the three Jagged slides |
| 4 | the bit table, combine / check / add / revoke, listing granted flags, roles | the three Permission slides |
| 5 | every question's expected output | Questions Bank |

## Notes for the session

* **No overloading, no interfaces, no lambdas** — everything here uses only what the students have covered.
* Two lines are commented out on purpose, to uncomment live so the class sees the error:
  * `ArrayExamplesDemo` — assigning to a `foreach` loop variable.
  * In `JaggedArrayDemo`, call `.Length` on the row that was never created and show the `NullReferenceException`.
* The `Resize` demo is the one worth spending time on: keep a second variable pointing at the array, resize through the first one, and print both lengths.
* `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture` is set in `Main` so averages print as `80.00`, not `80,00`.
